Pre-build the `pageRendersById`, `mappingsByRowId`, and `mappingsByQuestionKey` indexes once here before entering the loop, and pass them to `renderReadiness` to avoid O(N * M) overhead.

```javascript
  const pageRendersById = indexBy(asArray(renderManifest?.page_renders), (render) => render?.source_page_render_id);
  const mappingsByRowId = indexBy(asArray(renderManifest?.row_mappings), (mapping) => mapping?.precise_crop_source_map_row_id);
  const mappingsByQuestionKey = indexBy(asArray(renderManifest?.row_mappings), (mapping) => mapping?.question_key);

  for (const row of sourceRows) {
    if (!row?.question_key || completedWave1QuestionKeys.has(row.question_key)) continue;
    const render = renderReadiness(row, pageRendersById, mappingsByRowId, mappingsByQuestionKey);
